      "layer": "body",
      "route": "DIGITAL",
      "source": "text_layer",
      "label": "text",
      "text": "PK similarity between ABP 654, US-Stelara and EU-Stelara has been demonstrated in a 3-arm, parallel PK similarity study in healthy subjects (Study 20190230). PK samples were collected pre-dose on Day 1, and post-dose at 8 hr and 24 hr and on Days 3, 7, 9, 11, 13, 21, 28, 35, 49, 56, 70, 98 and 112. The point estimates and 90% &,V of the GMRs of PK parameters (AUC0-inf, Cmax and AUClast) were all within the pre-defined criteria of 0.8 to 1.25 (Table 8). The mean serum concentration-time profiles were similar between the ABP 654, US-Stelara and EU-Stelara treatment groups (Figure 2). The PK parameters following a single dose of ABP 654, US-Stelara and EU-Stelara are summarized in Table 8. In general, PK parameters and inter-subject variability were comparable across the three treatment groups.",
      "status": "kept"
    },
